1://! EMQX ExHook v3 HookProvider gRPC service implementation.
2://!
3://! EMQX acts as a gRPC client, calling this service for MQTT events
4://! The pinned EMQX 6.2.2 broker requires `emqx.exhook.v3`.
5://! The implementation records events through MutationEngine for
6://! accountability. Publish decisions are left to the broker (`IGNORE`) — the
7://! hook is an audit tap; identity gating stays with the Ghostbridge
8://! interceptor on the plugin surface. The one exception is the doorbell
9://! (`wake_doorbell`): clients whose id is an owner key must prove the
10://! matching SID1 against the identity sled, and may only subscribe to their
11://! own `opdbus/wake/<owner-key>` topic. Every other client is kept out of
12://! the `opdbus/` namespace and otherwise left to the broker's own rules.
